{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 4, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a nobleman and a leader of the County of Tripoli a Crusader state in the Holy Land. He was born in 1140 and died in 1187. Raymond was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. *## Early Life and Reign* Raymond III succeeded his father as Count of Tripoli at a young age after his father's assassination in 1152. His mother Hodierna acted as regent until he came of age. Raymond was taken captive by Nur ad-Din Zangi in 1164 during the Battle of Harim and was held prisoner for nearly a decade until his release in 1174. During his captivity the County of Tripoli was governed by Amalric I King of Jerusalem.\n\nAfter his release from captivity Raymond returned to Tripoli and began to consolidate his power. He married Eschiva of Bures Princess of Galilee and became involved in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem. *### Marriage and Alliances* Raymond's marriage to Eschiva brought him significant influence and power in the Kingdom of Jerusalem. He became a close ally of King Amalric and was involved in several military campaigns against the Zengid and Ayyubid dynasties. Raymond was also a cousin of King Baldwin IV and played an important role in the regency council during the king's minority.\n\nIn 1180 Raymond was appointed regent for King Baldwin IV who was suffering from leprosy. *## Regency and Later Life* As regent Raymond worked to strengthen the Kingdom of Jerusalem and secure its borders. He was a skilled military leader and diplomat and was able to negotiate a truce with Saladin the Ayyubid sultan. However Raymond's regency was marked by power struggles with other nobles and the influence of the Catholic Church. Raymond's term as regent ended in 1181 when Baldwin IV came of age. He continued to play an important role in the Kingdom of Jerusalem until his death in 1187. Raymond die